expect
  # The released ground jump is cut short and the air jump follows; the first cling since the floor
  # restores it once more. After that every press is either a kick at an apex (on the cling frame,
  # from the buffer) or waits for one: kicks are fixed and restore nothing, so mashing climbs one
  # full kick per apex, 24 frames apart, exactly like timed kicks.
  at 6 event.air_jump=1
  at 13 event.wall_kick=1
  at 18 event.air_jump=1
  at 25 event.wall_kick=1
  at 49 event.wall_kick=1
  at 73 event.wall_kick=1
  never 19..129 event.air_jump=1
  # Over the top, a few frames after the timed climb (whose full first jump rises higher).
  mark top 74..129 event.land=1
  at top y=192u state=ground
end
